What are Small Scale Carbon Capture Systems?
Small Scale Carbon Capture Systems represent a critical solution for distributed emission sources, capturing between 10 to 10,000 tons of CO₂ annually. These modular units employ various technologies including amine scrubbing, membrane separation, and solid sorbent adsorption to serve applications ranging from industrial boilers to marine vessels. Unlike large centralized capture facilities, these systems offer operational flexibility and faster deployment timelines - crucial advantages in today's rapidly evolving decarbonization landscape.

